/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/sort.k-3-// for kprove (a trusted primitive, correctness/ordering proved in Lean / notes/sort-probe),
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/sort.k-4-// and a concrete insertion sort for krun. Wrappers verify the logic AROUND the sort (index /
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/sort.k:5:// slice / filter / dedup); indexing an opaque sortVS(VS) carries through as an opaque term, so
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/sort.k:6:// no ordering lemma is needed in K — the trust (sortVS = real sorted) is discharged by each
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/sort.k-7-// problem's differential test. Only int lists (compared by projectIntTotal); keyed / string
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/sort.k-8-// sorts are separate. Fires only via the "sorted" builtin, so inert for non-sorting programs.
